WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.810
Security teams rely heavily on alerts generated by SIEMs, EDR platforms, firewalls,

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.685
and other security technologies.

00:00:06.685 --> 00:00:07.760
Those tools are important,

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.985
but they do not reveal every important security event automatically.

00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:14.480
Some threats may use legitimate tools, valid credentials, novel techniques,

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.845
or low-and-slow approaches designed to blend into normal activity.

00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:20.665
If defenders only investigate what already triggered an alert,

00:00:20.665 --> 00:00:23.135
hidden activity may remain unnoticed.

00:00:23.135 --> 00:00:26.360
Threat hunting exists because defenders cannot assume that everything important will

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.215
appear in an alert queue.

00:00:28.215 --> 00:00:31.695
Hunting is a proactive effort to search for suspicious activity that may have gone

00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:33.490
undetected by existing controls.

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:38.335
A mature SOC uses alerts, investigations, incident response, detection engineering,

00:00:38.335 --> 00:00:40.435
threat intelligence, and hunting together.

00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:43.000
Hunting helps the team ask better questions, test assumptions,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.600
and improve visibility over time.
